1
00:00:04,204 --> 00:00:06,206
We have an emergency.

2
00:00:08,108 --> 00:00:11,144
Chairman Uchikanda's daughter

3
00:00:11,611 --> 00:00:12,746
has cancer.

4
00:00:14,748 --> 00:00:18,685
But he doesn't have
a daughter, does he?

5
00:00:19,652 --> 00:00:20,653
Actually...

6
00:00:33,767 --> 00:00:35,402
The cancer patient is

7
00:00:35,468 --> 00:00:39,873
Chairman Uchikanda and
his wife's beloved daughter

8
00:00:40,640 --> 00:00:43,376
Nana Uchikanda.

9
00:00:43,777 --> 00:00:44,644
A dog?

10
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:47,347
Not just any dog.
The chairman's daughter.

11
00:00:48,081 --> 00:00:50,650
But animals are outside
our field of expertise.

12
00:00:50,984 --> 00:00:53,686
He should consult a veterinarian.

13
00:00:53,820 --> 00:00:55,889
We have one.

14
00:00:56,689 --> 00:01:00,927
A tough female surgeon who'd
operate on any living creature

15
00:01:01,361 --> 00:01:03,229
suffering from a disease.

16
00:01:05,698 --> 00:01:06,866
She never fails.

17
00:01:11,871 --> 00:01:13,907
A 5-cm tumor
in the right lobe of the liver.

18
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:15,075
Hepatectomy.

19
00:01:15,208 --> 00:01:16,176
Mercedes incision.

20
00:01:16,276 --> 00:01:18,711
A midline incision is
the norm for dogs.

21
00:01:18,912 --> 00:01:21,314
And it's too late to operate.

22
00:01:21,381 --> 00:01:24,951
The high level of visceral fat
inhibits a midline incision.

23
00:01:25,085 --> 00:01:26,319
Let's do it. Scalpel.

24
00:01:34,327 --> 00:01:36,996
Rest assured, Mrs. Uchikanda.

25
00:01:37,197 --> 00:01:40,200
Michiko Daimon, who was
appointed by my husband

26
00:01:40,800 --> 00:01:44,237
has a bad personality but
she's a skilled surgeon.

27
00:01:44,304 --> 00:01:46,072
I see. Mrs. Hiruma...

28
00:01:46,573 --> 00:01:48,274
you didn't have to come.

29
00:01:48,341 --> 00:01:50,009
But I wanted to.

30
00:01:50,076 --> 00:01:51,978
I'm also worried about Nana.

31
00:01:52,679 --> 00:01:56,149
I'm praying with you for
a successful surgery.

32
00:01:57,584 --> 00:01:59,953
Michiko Daimon, how did it go?

33
00:02:00,019 --> 00:02:00,920
How's Nana?

34
00:02:01,488 --> 00:02:05,525
The tumor was completely removed.
She can go home in three days.

35
00:02:05,658 --> 00:02:07,160
Wonderful.

36
00:02:07,660 --> 00:02:09,963
Congratulations.

37
00:02:10,029 --> 00:02:11,030
Nicely handled.

38
00:02:11,831 --> 00:02:15,268
We'll celebrate with Nana's favorite meal,
marbled meat.

39
00:02:15,335 --> 00:02:18,071
A diet like that made her sick.

40
00:02:18,838 --> 00:02:22,142
The poor dog is a victim
of her owner's ego.

41
00:02:22,475 --> 00:02:23,510
What did she say?

42
00:02:23,676 --> 00:02:24,744
Michiko Daimon!

43
00:02:25,612 --> 00:02:28,181
How dare you be so rude
to Mrs. Uchikanda.

44
00:02:28,281 --> 00:02:30,283
- Apologize.
- I decline.

45
00:02:30,617 --> 00:02:34,287
<i>This is the story of</i>
<i>a lone wolf woman doctor.</i>

46
00:02:34,354 --> 00:02:37,891
Ear, ear, ear. Touch my ear.

47
00:02:38,091 --> 00:02:41,361
Blow, blow, blow in my ear.

48
00:02:41,928 --> 00:02:44,063
Stop it...

49
00:02:44,130 --> 00:02:45,798
Shut up.

50
00:02:46,766 --> 00:02:47,734
He's so annoying.

51
00:02:47,901 --> 00:02:49,202
He's saying something.

52
00:02:49,269 --> 00:02:50,870
Don't mind that stupid robot.

53
00:02:54,107 --> 00:02:55,608
Hi, honey.

54
00:02:58,478 --> 00:03:00,013
- What?
- Nothing.

55
00:03:01,281 --> 00:03:04,217
Hana, you're family to me but

56
00:03:04,517 --> 00:03:06,686
an outsider to this hospital.

57
00:03:06,886 --> 00:03:09,656
You can't barge in here
without an appointment.

58
00:03:09,856 --> 00:03:12,325
Hello, Director Hiruma.

59
00:03:12,759 --> 00:03:14,260
Mrs. Uchikanda.

60
00:03:14,527 --> 00:03:17,430
How nice to see you.
Please come in.

61
00:03:17,764 --> 00:03:20,633
Nana's surgery was successful.

62
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:23,937
That's marvelous news.

63
00:03:24,003 --> 00:03:26,940
Miss Nakatani, we'll have tea.

64
00:03:27,006 --> 00:03:27,874
Thank you.

65
00:03:27,941 --> 00:03:29,142
You're most welcome.

66
00:03:29,209 --> 00:03:30,710
A thank-you gift from my husband.

67
00:03:31,077 --> 00:03:32,245
Wow.

68
00:03:32,478 --> 00:03:33,813
A photo book?

69
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:35,248
Fantastic.

70
00:03:35,481 --> 00:03:38,952
I am what I am today thanks to

71
00:03:39,118 --> 00:03:40,653
you and the chairman.

72
00:03:41,020 --> 00:03:43,356
You don't have to thank me.

73
00:03:43,790 --> 00:03:45,725
I'm an outsider after all.

74
00:03:46,092 --> 00:03:47,427
<i>In 2017</i>

75
00:03:47,961 --> 00:03:53,266
<i>the university medical system</i>
<i>regained its once-lost authority</i>

76
00:03:53,566 --> 00:03:59,572
<i>and the system on which lives depend</i>
<i>strayed away from what it should be.</i>

77
00:04:00,039 --> 00:04:02,242
I have another favor.

78
00:04:02,308 --> 00:04:05,178
Do you? Just name it.

79
00:04:08,114 --> 00:04:09,582
My cousin.

80
00:04:10,283 --> 00:04:12,752
She's shy and hasn't found a husband yet.

81
00:04:13,987 --> 00:04:17,690
Is there a nice single doctor
at this hospital?

82
00:04:17,757 --> 00:04:19,058
For an arranged marriage?

83
00:04:19,492 --> 00:04:21,327
May I see the photo?

84
00:04:21,461 --> 00:04:22,562
Thank you.

85
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:31,204
Oh my…She looks lovely
in a red kimono.

86
00:04:32,372 --> 00:04:33,906
Doesn't she?

87
00:04:34,340 --> 00:04:35,375
<i>In the midst of this,</i>

88
00:04:35,475 --> 00:04:38,745
<i>doctors free from any</i>
<i>establishment emerged.</i>

89
00:04:39,012 --> 00:04:42,849
<i>Freelance doctors, in other words,</i>
<i>lone wolf doctors.</i>

90
00:04:43,483 --> 00:04:44,317
Dr. Demon.

91
00:04:45,251 --> 00:04:48,588
You're Dr. Demon, aren't you?

92
00:04:49,188 --> 00:04:51,157
I'm Michiko Daimon, a surgeon.

93
00:04:52,091 --> 00:04:57,497
I knew it. Stubborn, sharp-tongued,
terrible personality.

94
00:04:57,563 --> 00:04:59,165
But Japan's best surgeon.

95
00:04:59,232 --> 00:05:00,366
Who are you?

96
00:05:00,533 --> 00:05:03,503
I've been dying to meet you.
I'm so happy.

97
00:05:03,569 --> 00:05:05,338
Can I hug you?

98
00:05:06,906 --> 00:05:08,608
<i>This woman, for example.</i>

99
00:05:09,309 --> 00:05:12,845
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

100
00:05:13,279 --> 00:05:18,117
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

101
00:05:18,518 --> 00:05:19,585
Who are you?

102
00:05:22,055 --> 00:05:24,324
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

103
00:05:24,824 --> 00:05:25,825
<i>Also known as...</i>

104
00:05:26,392 --> 00:05:28,094
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

105
00:05:43,576 --> 00:05:44,711
Nice to see you again.

106
00:05:47,814 --> 00:05:48,781
Please sit.

107
00:05:58,124 --> 00:06:04,163
This is Dr. Mamoru Hara,
a surgeon at Totei University Hospital.

108
00:06:04,364 --> 00:06:06,666
I'm Mamoru Hara.
Pleasure to meet you.

109
00:06:09,402 --> 00:06:11,037
My cousin Momoka.

110
00:06:16,175 --> 00:06:19,879
Arranged marriage with
Mrs. Uchikanda's cousin?

111
00:06:20,012 --> 00:06:21,748
Director Hiruma named him.

112
00:06:21,814 --> 00:06:24,117
He happens to be the right age.

113
00:06:24,283 --> 00:06:25,151
Happens to be?

114
00:06:26,252 --> 00:06:30,189
Dr. Hara finally has his opportunity.

115
00:06:30,656 --> 00:06:33,893
If things go well, he would be
a relative of the chairman.

116
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:36,062
Not a bad deal.

117
00:06:36,195 --> 00:06:40,133
Does every doctor want to marry
someone from an important family?

118
00:06:41,868 --> 00:06:43,503
Not everyone.

119
00:06:45,304 --> 00:06:46,472
How about you?

120
00:06:47,874 --> 00:06:50,710
Do you want to get married
in the first place?

121
00:06:53,813 --> 00:06:54,647
So...

122
00:06:56,215 --> 00:06:58,751
Check that patient's blood pressure.

123
00:07:03,589 --> 00:07:06,759
I graduated from Totei University

124
00:07:07,059 --> 00:07:10,563
and became a surgeon at
its main and satellite hospitals.

125
00:07:10,630 --> 00:07:12,598
I was also posted to Russia.

126
00:07:12,732 --> 00:07:17,003
I successfully performed many
difficult surgeries there.

127
00:07:17,069 --> 00:07:18,938
If I may say so myself.

128
00:07:20,473 --> 00:07:22,308
Do you have any hobbies?

129
00:07:25,678 --> 00:07:29,682
Momoka, why don't you and
Dr. Hara go for a walk?

130
00:07:29,749 --> 00:07:31,717
That's a good idea.

131
00:07:31,784 --> 00:07:35,254
Yes, it is.
Shall we, Momoka?

132
00:07:35,321 --> 00:07:36,289
Hold on.

133
00:07:38,591 --> 00:07:39,859
Dr. Daimon.

134
00:07:39,926 --> 00:07:41,761
What are you doing here?

135
00:07:42,195 --> 00:07:44,263
- Kin has a visitor.
- What?

136
00:07:49,969 --> 00:07:51,537
- Mamo...
- Nana...

137
00:07:51,737 --> 00:07:52,572
Mamo...?

138
00:07:52,705 --> 00:07:54,006
I found you at last.

139
00:07:58,277 --> 00:08:00,780
Excuse me.
Who are you?

140
00:08:01,681 --> 00:08:04,116
I'm Nanasha Najinsky.

141
00:08:04,450 --> 00:08:05,885
Mamo's girlfriend.

142
00:08:07,453 --> 00:08:08,721
Are you serious?

143
00:08:16,429 --> 00:08:17,663
What's going on?

144
00:08:18,598 --> 00:08:20,266
What's going on,
Michiko Daimon?!

145
00:08:21,501 --> 00:08:24,504
She said she'll treat me to dinner
if I brought her here.

146
00:08:25,338 --> 00:08:27,173
I have an operation.

147
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:29,475
Dr. Daimon…Hey...

148
00:08:29,942 --> 00:08:31,811
Nana…Wait...

149
00:08:36,382 --> 00:08:38,251
- Mamo...
- Yes?

150
00:08:38,317 --> 00:08:39,552
Explain yourself.

151
00:08:40,453 --> 00:08:45,525
She was my girlfriend when
I was posted to Russia.

152
00:08:46,325 --> 00:08:50,162
But she broke up with me.

153
00:08:50,229 --> 00:08:52,865
I came back to Japan soon after...

154
00:08:52,932 --> 00:08:54,100
Stop making excuses!

155
00:08:54,166 --> 00:08:55,034
I'm sorry.

156
00:08:55,902 --> 00:08:57,370
Mamo...

157
00:08:58,304 --> 00:09:01,541
You made Mrs. Uchikanda lose face.

158
00:09:04,143 --> 00:09:08,648
The chairman must be furious
with you as well.

159
00:09:08,748 --> 00:09:09,916
Oh no...

160
00:09:11,751 --> 00:09:14,086
She blames us too

161
00:09:15,521 --> 00:09:17,590
for introducing you.

162
00:09:17,790 --> 00:09:19,325
You damn fool!

163
00:09:20,860 --> 00:09:23,696
Break up with Nanasha right away

164
00:09:24,030 --> 00:09:26,299
and set things straight.

165
00:09:26,365 --> 00:09:27,199
Yes sir.

166
00:09:32,171 --> 00:09:33,739
Like I said

167
00:09:33,806 --> 00:09:36,409
if we operate now,
you'll be cured.

168
00:09:36,676 --> 00:09:39,912
But I heard the scar hurts after surgery.

169
00:09:39,979 --> 00:09:42,014
Of course it does.
We cut your stomach.

170
00:09:42,782 --> 00:09:44,584
You'll die without surgery.

171
00:09:44,650 --> 00:09:45,885
Dr. Daimon, compliance...

172
00:09:46,319 --> 00:09:48,354
What if you fail?

173
00:09:48,487 --> 00:09:50,256
I never fail.

174
00:09:51,057 --> 00:09:52,858
How can you be sure?

175
00:10:04,704 --> 00:10:09,675
Dr. Daimon will probably use
a laparoscope for this.

176
00:10:11,177 --> 00:10:13,613
Small scar. Less pain.

177
00:10:14,614 --> 00:10:15,615
Is that true?

178
00:10:16,882 --> 00:10:17,717
Yes.

179
00:10:19,218 --> 00:10:20,753
I know you're scared.

180
00:10:21,153 --> 00:10:24,757
But Dr. Daimon is a brilliant surgeon.

181
00:10:25,057 --> 00:10:27,293
Thank you for encouraging me.

182
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:30,329
Wow. But who is she?

183
00:10:31,263 --> 00:10:32,498
Kin's girlfriend.

184
00:10:33,332 --> 00:10:34,233
I'm not kidding.

185
00:10:34,867 --> 00:10:36,502
I know you'll be fine.

186
00:10:51,450 --> 00:10:52,551
So you're a surgeon.

187
00:10:53,452 --> 00:10:55,021
I used to be.

188
00:10:55,187 --> 00:10:56,889
I quit being a surgeon.

189
00:10:57,256 --> 00:10:58,090
Quit?

190
00:10:59,125 --> 00:11:00,793
Dr. Daimon...

191
00:11:02,128 --> 00:11:03,295
You're mistaken.

192
00:11:03,996 --> 00:11:04,830
What?

193
00:11:05,197 --> 00:11:06,932
You said you never fail.

194
00:11:07,066 --> 00:11:10,636
Don't say that when you don't
know how the patient feels.

195
00:11:11,203 --> 00:11:15,975
A real doctor has to be there
emotionally for the patient.

196
00:11:16,442 --> 00:11:17,309
Why?

197
00:11:18,577 --> 00:11:20,112
Why did you quit being a surgeon?

198
00:11:20,913 --> 00:11:23,516
Your face lights up when you talk surgery.

199
00:11:29,855 --> 00:11:32,258
You're in a very precarious
position right now.

200
00:11:33,159 --> 00:11:38,431
If you choose Nanasha,
you'll ruin your career forever.

201
00:11:39,432 --> 00:11:42,201
A valuable opinion by Dr. Torii

202
00:11:42,401 --> 00:11:45,037
who was suspended for his revolt.

203
00:11:47,807 --> 00:11:51,577
Break it off with her immediately
if you wish to stay here.

204
00:11:53,713 --> 00:11:54,547
There he is.

205
00:11:55,381 --> 00:11:56,315
Mamo...

206
00:11:56,382 --> 00:11:58,250
Why do you keep bringing her?

207
00:11:58,384 --> 00:11:59,852
It's 5 PM. I'm going home.

208
00:11:59,919 --> 00:12:00,853
Are you listening?

209
00:12:02,888 --> 00:12:03,956
Dr. Morimoto?

210
00:12:04,290 --> 00:12:09,128
An American surgeon
Dr. Hara met in Russia.

211
00:12:09,195 --> 00:12:10,730
Are they still a couple?

212
00:12:10,796 --> 00:12:13,899
You're still working at this hour?

213
00:12:14,567 --> 00:12:16,368
The Japanese work too much.

214
00:12:30,483 --> 00:12:31,550
Why did you quit?

215
00:12:32,518 --> 00:12:35,254
You said you found
purpose in life as a doctor.

216
00:12:36,989 --> 00:12:39,225
I quit to be with you.

217
00:12:39,825 --> 00:12:42,394
For me? Are you serious?

218
00:12:42,461 --> 00:12:44,663
Breaking up with you
was a mistake.

219
00:12:45,231 --> 00:12:47,299
This time, I won't leave you.

220
00:12:54,039 --> 00:12:56,408
I love "oden."

221
00:13:00,312 --> 00:13:01,147
What's the matter?

222
00:13:05,251 --> 00:13:08,320
Nana, it's not a good time
right now.

223
00:13:09,288 --> 00:13:11,257
Actually, not just now...

224
00:13:12,358 --> 00:13:13,292
You see...

225
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:16,629
I might get married.

226
00:13:22,067 --> 00:13:26,806
Do you honestly love this person?

227
00:13:28,541 --> 00:13:30,876
Well…Um...

228
00:13:37,383 --> 00:13:38,951
Another bottle, please.

229
00:13:39,151 --> 00:13:39,985
Sure.

230
00:13:41,020 --> 00:13:41,854
Fine then.

231
00:13:43,756 --> 00:13:44,757
I understand.

232
00:13:45,224 --> 00:13:48,460
But I'm going to stay in Japan
for three months.

233
00:13:48,527 --> 00:13:51,197
Be with me just for that time.

234
00:13:52,064 --> 00:13:54,700
Let's go on lots of dates.

235
00:13:55,134 --> 00:13:57,536
We'll go places and
eat good food.

236
00:13:57,603 --> 00:13:58,537
Nana, no.

237
00:14:01,841 --> 00:14:03,809
Don't be so selfish.
It's too late.

238
00:14:06,412 --> 00:14:10,382
Don't make my heart sway.

239
00:14:17,223 --> 00:14:19,158
It's just like you to say that.

240
00:14:20,159 --> 00:14:22,895
Even after all these years

241
00:14:23,529 --> 00:14:25,264
I still love you.

242
00:14:30,302 --> 00:14:31,136
Excuse me.

243
00:14:31,670 --> 00:14:34,340
Can I have a "konnyaku"?

244
00:14:35,174 --> 00:14:38,444
She traveled all the way
across the sea to see you.

245
00:14:38,577 --> 00:14:42,014
But you shouldn't have taken
her to his blind date.

246
00:14:42,081 --> 00:14:44,049
She said she'd buy me dinner.

247
00:14:44,116 --> 00:14:44,950
Pon.

248
00:14:45,150 --> 00:14:47,887
It's all your fault, Dr. Daimon.

249
00:14:48,020 --> 00:14:49,755
Why are you here tonight?

250
00:14:49,822 --> 00:14:53,492
Dr. Jonouchi accompanied
Dr. Ebina on his business trip.

251
00:14:53,659 --> 00:14:56,295
I thought I'd fill in for her.

252
00:14:56,428 --> 00:15:00,432
She didn't want to go but
the pay was astonishing.

253
00:15:01,433 --> 00:15:04,570
What if she and Dr. Ebina
hook up over there?

254
00:15:05,537 --> 00:15:09,174
I don't understand women.
Why now?

255
00:15:09,708 --> 00:15:11,410
I left my feelings for her in Russia.

256
00:15:11,543 --> 00:15:12,711
You're swaying.

257
00:15:12,845 --> 00:15:16,248
But it's either her or the hospital.

258
00:15:16,315 --> 00:15:17,883
So I thought about it.

259
00:15:18,550 --> 00:15:22,888
If I get fired from Totei,
I'd like to be registered here.

260
00:15:23,155 --> 00:15:24,990
We only manage skilled doctors.

261
00:15:25,124 --> 00:15:26,959
- I know.
- You're not skilled.

262
00:15:27,026 --> 00:15:28,360
That's a low blow.

263
00:15:28,427 --> 00:15:29,995
Annoying. Pon.

264
00:15:30,262 --> 00:15:32,031
Looks like a big hand.

265
00:15:32,398 --> 00:15:36,201
Why did Nanasha quit
being a doctor?

266
00:15:36,268 --> 00:15:37,102
Puzzling, right?

267
00:15:37,236 --> 00:15:39,238
She quit to come see me.

268
00:15:39,405 --> 00:15:42,308
A top-notch American surgeon?

269
00:15:42,374 --> 00:15:44,810
Can you imagine that?

270
00:15:44,877 --> 00:15:46,045
I can't.

271
00:15:46,145 --> 00:15:47,813
You guys are mean.

272
00:15:50,516 --> 00:15:51,951
The unimaginable just happened.

273
00:15:52,551 --> 00:15:53,786
Ron!

274
00:15:54,486 --> 00:15:56,722
"Dai-san-gen"!

275
00:15:56,789 --> 00:15:59,391
Oh no!!

276
00:16:02,461 --> 00:16:04,129
Nanasha Najinsky.

277
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:07,566
A Stanbridge professor
at her age.

278
00:16:10,302 --> 00:16:12,504
She has an amazing track record.

279
00:16:12,871 --> 00:16:14,840
What a waste of surgical skill.

280
00:16:16,308 --> 00:16:17,142
What is it?

281
00:16:17,343 --> 00:16:19,244
This last operation.

282
00:16:23,716 --> 00:16:25,918
What? Medical error?

283
00:16:27,453 --> 00:16:31,357
"There was a failed heart surgery
and the lead surgeon was

284
00:16:31,890 --> 00:16:32,958
Nanasha Najinsky."

285
00:16:33,926 --> 00:16:35,027
Let me see...

286
00:16:36,328 --> 00:16:38,297
"When suturing the incisions

287
00:16:39,064 --> 00:16:41,266
the phrenic nerve was
accidentally damaged."

288
00:16:42,134 --> 00:16:44,236
It's not a difficult suture.

289
00:16:44,570 --> 00:16:45,871
Did the patient die?

290
00:16:46,372 --> 00:16:48,307
The patient…No.

291
00:16:49,174 --> 00:16:51,577
He survived but suffers
from side effects.

292
00:16:51,643 --> 00:16:52,945
He's suing the hospital.

293
00:16:53,846 --> 00:16:57,116
Did she quit because of this?

294
00:16:57,282 --> 00:17:00,586
Not quit. Maybe she was fired.

295
00:17:04,189 --> 00:17:05,024
Nana...

296
00:17:08,427 --> 00:17:14,299
I brought some souvenirs
for you all but...

297
00:17:16,935 --> 00:17:19,872
I see it's a bad time.

298
00:17:22,307 --> 00:17:23,142
Nana.

299
00:17:23,909 --> 00:17:25,110
Sorry, Dr. Hara.

300
00:17:25,677 --> 00:17:26,678
Bad timing.

301
00:17:26,745 --> 00:17:28,213
Don't do that.

302
00:17:35,754 --> 00:17:38,357
Is it true about
your surgical error?

303
00:17:40,025 --> 00:17:43,095
Your operations were always flawless.
What went wrong?

304
00:17:45,330 --> 00:17:46,865
It's my fault.

305
00:17:47,566 --> 00:17:49,401
I can't apologize enough to the patient.

306
00:17:51,303 --> 00:17:53,872
Was it the real reason
you quit?

307
00:17:53,939 --> 00:17:55,207
And why you're here?

308
00:17:55,274 --> 00:17:56,141
Mamo...

309
00:17:57,109 --> 00:17:58,544
I have to tell you something.

310
00:17:59,445 --> 00:18:00,312
Hey.

311
00:18:01,146 --> 00:18:03,649
- I want to run some tests.
- What?

312
00:18:07,186 --> 00:18:10,255
A 7-cm tumor in
the left frontal lobe.

313
00:18:10,322 --> 00:18:12,691
Adjacent to the motor cortex
and possibly invasive.

314
00:18:13,659 --> 00:18:14,493
Oh my God...

315
00:18:16,328 --> 00:18:17,162
Nana...

316
00:18:19,531 --> 00:18:20,432
Did you know?

317
00:18:24,036 --> 00:18:28,674
You failed your last operation
because your hand was trembling.

318
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:31,810
It bothered me when I saw you...

319
00:18:32,411 --> 00:18:34,379
I know you'll be fine.

320
00:18:43,589 --> 00:18:44,590
Yes.

321
00:18:45,357 --> 00:18:48,026
But I wanted to save the patient.

322
00:18:48,694 --> 00:18:49,995
Don't underestimate operations.

323
00:18:51,597 --> 00:18:55,734
How would you feel if you were
the one being operated on?

324
00:18:57,436 --> 00:18:58,670
You don't deserve to be a surgeon.

325
00:19:02,441 --> 00:19:03,442
You're right.

326
00:19:07,045 --> 00:19:08,714
That's why I quit.

327
00:19:16,788 --> 00:19:19,091
I failed as a doctor

328
00:19:20,559 --> 00:19:22,227
and became a patient.

329
00:19:25,230 --> 00:19:26,198
Then...

330
00:19:28,901 --> 00:19:30,702
I thought of you.

331
00:19:31,770 --> 00:19:35,040
When your patients had children

332
00:19:35,240 --> 00:19:38,076
you worried about who
would cook their meals.

333
00:19:39,378 --> 00:19:44,716
You helped a couple reconcile
when a disease was

334
00:19:45,384 --> 00:19:48,520
tearing their marriage apart.

335
00:19:48,921 --> 00:19:51,823
You were always there for the patients.

336
00:19:53,559 --> 00:19:54,960
You were a real doctor.

337
00:19:57,863 --> 00:20:02,367
I was hoping you'd be
there for me too.

338
00:20:09,508 --> 00:20:10,609
Let me cut it.

339
00:20:16,848 --> 00:20:18,417
This operation is infeasible.

340
00:20:20,052 --> 00:20:23,622
I want to spend
my last days with you.

341
00:20:24,356 --> 00:20:25,924
But Nana...

342
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:53,085
We saw the images.

343
00:20:53,185 --> 00:20:55,254
Complete removal of the tumor
is extremely difficult.

344
00:20:55,520 --> 00:21:00,392
Even a minor damage to the motor
cortex will affect her motor skills.

345
00:21:00,459 --> 00:21:02,394
She doesn't want an operation, right?

346
00:21:02,794 --> 00:21:05,964
She won't last three months.
I'll operate on her.

347
00:21:06,031 --> 00:21:07,065
Dr. Hara...

348
00:21:07,199 --> 00:21:10,002
Why don't you take some time off?

349
00:21:11,069 --> 00:21:14,573
She wants to spend time
with you, doesn't she?

350
00:21:15,440 --> 00:21:20,479
Then do what she wants.
Be there for her.

351
00:21:20,646 --> 00:21:21,613
Does this mean...

352
00:21:23,115 --> 00:21:24,316
Don't worry.

353
00:21:25,183 --> 00:21:28,253
You can come back when it's over.

354
00:21:28,320 --> 00:21:29,154
Wait a second.

355
00:21:29,221 --> 00:21:31,790
You're still an instructor.

356
00:21:32,357 --> 00:21:35,894
Isn't it about time you become
an associate professor?

357
00:21:35,961 --> 00:21:36,962
I said I'll operate.

358
00:21:37,062 --> 00:21:39,364
Keep your mouth shut!

359
00:21:39,498 --> 00:21:42,000
You're an outsider with this case.

360
00:21:42,167 --> 00:21:43,635
Stay out of it.

361
00:21:44,069 --> 00:21:47,339
Dr. Hara, an insider,
what's your answer?

362
00:21:49,908 --> 00:21:50,742
Dr. Hara?

363
00:21:56,882 --> 00:21:58,350
- Yes sir...
- What?!

364
00:22:01,453 --> 00:22:02,521
Yes sir.

365
00:22:04,956 --> 00:22:05,791
It's settled then.

366
00:22:07,993 --> 00:22:12,364
I'm honoring Nana's wish to
spend her last days with me.

367
00:22:12,664 --> 00:22:16,401
I'm going to be there for her
until the very end.

368
00:22:17,936 --> 00:22:18,770
Hey.

369
00:22:20,405 --> 00:22:21,907
You call yourself a doctor?

370
00:22:24,176 --> 00:22:27,946
Being there for a patient
doesn't cure the disease.

371
00:22:38,390 --> 00:22:40,225
BEN CASEY

372
00:22:40,692 --> 00:22:43,995
Nanasha has an impressive background.

373
00:22:47,599 --> 00:22:51,803
She's the daughter of the American
Medical Club's vice chairman.

374
00:22:52,037 --> 00:22:52,871
What's that?

375
00:22:53,372 --> 00:22:55,474
The leaders of the American
medical community.

376
00:22:56,007 --> 00:22:57,209
Too bad.

377
00:22:57,542 --> 00:23:02,381
I could've charged her operation
to the American bigwigs.

378
00:23:04,683 --> 00:23:06,051
When you found out

379
00:23:07,219 --> 00:23:11,556
about your disease, did you
want someone there for you?

380
00:23:12,391 --> 00:23:13,625
I don't remember.

381
00:23:15,026 --> 00:23:19,831
But I do remember that
you weren't there for me.

382
00:23:20,332 --> 00:23:22,467
You ran away.

383
00:23:22,534 --> 00:23:23,635
Yes, I did.

384
00:23:23,702 --> 00:23:25,837
Hello, Ben Casey.

385
00:23:27,372 --> 00:23:31,410
But I knew how operations
could go horribly wrong.

386
00:23:32,310 --> 00:23:34,479
So I didn't want you to do it.

387
00:23:40,852 --> 00:23:42,754
Nanasha…Hello.

388
00:23:43,155 --> 00:23:46,024
Good evening.
I'm sorry to intrude.

389
00:23:46,625 --> 00:23:49,661
I wanted to say goodbye
to Dr. Daimon.

390
00:23:50,262 --> 00:23:53,365
Mamo and I are leaving
Tokyo tomorrow.

391
00:23:55,667 --> 00:23:57,302
You're making a mistake.

392
00:23:58,103 --> 00:24:00,739
A surgeon giving up on her own life?

393
00:24:01,706 --> 00:24:06,344
I know this is for the best
because I'm a surgeon.

394
00:24:06,745 --> 00:24:10,015
I'm glad I met you.

395
00:24:21,326 --> 00:24:25,363
Mamo will return to the hospital
in about three months.

396
00:24:26,498 --> 00:24:29,634
Please take care of him.

397
00:24:43,615 --> 00:24:46,384
As you all know

398
00:24:46,785 --> 00:24:52,491
heeding my advice,
Dr. Hara has decided to

399
00:24:52,858 --> 00:24:56,328
take a leave of absence.

400
00:24:56,695 --> 00:25:02,000
His shoes aren't big to fill
but make sure they are.

401
00:25:02,067 --> 00:25:02,901
Yes sir.

402
00:25:03,335 --> 00:25:05,036
All right then.

403
00:25:05,570 --> 00:25:09,174
Let's make this
a productive conference.

404
00:25:09,407 --> 00:25:11,409
- Yes sir.
- Very nice.

405
00:25:11,476 --> 00:25:14,779
Let us begin
this week's pre-op conference.

406
00:25:14,980 --> 00:25:17,682
First case, Mr. Yosuke Akiyama.

407
00:25:21,386 --> 00:25:22,854
I can't wait to get to Kanazawa.

408
00:25:24,055 --> 00:25:27,592
Thank you for being here with me.

409
00:25:28,193 --> 00:25:30,595
I'm really happy.

410
00:25:32,264 --> 00:25:33,098
Yeah.

411
00:25:34,666 --> 00:25:37,702
There are so many things
I want to do.

412
00:25:39,604 --> 00:25:42,274
I want to eat delicious ramen noodles.

413
00:25:42,407 --> 00:25:45,377
I also want real sushi.

414
00:25:45,544 --> 00:25:47,646
And see the beautiful
Mount Fuji.

415
00:25:48,446 --> 00:25:51,316
Most of all, I want to see
the cherry blossoms.

416
00:25:53,552 --> 00:25:56,388
But that won't happen.

417
00:26:00,992 --> 00:26:04,829
Being there for a patient
doesn't cure the disease.

418
00:26:13,972 --> 00:26:14,806
What's the matter?

419
00:26:16,441 --> 00:26:17,642
Nothing.

420
00:26:18,777 --> 00:26:20,712
Let's get lunch when we arrive.

421
00:26:21,413 --> 00:26:22,247
Yes.

422
00:26:27,485 --> 00:26:31,489
Case 5, Mr. Shozo Murota,
age 68.

423
00:26:31,923 --> 00:26:35,927
Progressive colorectal cancer
in stage 3B.

424
00:26:35,994 --> 00:26:37,562
Lead surgeon, Dr. Daimon.

425
00:26:37,729 --> 00:26:38,597
Okay.

426
00:26:49,874 --> 00:26:50,709
Dr. Hara?

427
00:27:03,888 --> 00:27:05,690
What are you doing?

428
00:27:11,863 --> 00:27:15,600
Dr. Hara, what's going on?

429
00:27:18,570 --> 00:27:22,007
The patient is Nanasha Najinsky,
age 35.

430
00:27:22,207 --> 00:27:24,442
The diagnosis is brain tumor.

431
00:27:36,287 --> 00:27:37,188
Please...

432
00:27:38,590 --> 00:27:41,359
let me operate on Nana.

433
00:27:46,297 --> 00:27:47,899
You're on leave.

434
00:27:49,934 --> 00:27:52,037
Are you going against
the director's decision?

435
00:27:53,471 --> 00:27:55,640
I won't be needing any more days off.

436
00:28:01,312 --> 00:28:03,648
LETTER OF RESIGNATION

437
00:28:11,089 --> 00:28:14,426
She said she wants to see
the cherry blossoms.

438
00:28:17,195 --> 00:28:19,564
She wants to stay alive until spring.

439
00:28:22,300 --> 00:28:26,337
Just being there for a patient
who wants to stay alive...

440
00:28:28,139 --> 00:28:29,708
is not a doctor's job!

441
00:28:32,310 --> 00:28:34,212
As the best university hospital in Japan,

442
00:28:35,080 --> 00:28:36,214
we can save her!

443
00:28:37,215 --> 00:28:39,284
Dr. Inomata! Dr. Torii!

444
00:28:40,719 --> 00:28:41,786
If we can't do that...

445
00:28:44,055 --> 00:28:45,623
I can't stay here.

446
00:28:46,991 --> 00:28:47,926
So please.

447
00:28:49,494 --> 00:28:51,262
In exchange for this

448
00:28:52,464 --> 00:28:54,332
let me operate on her.

449
00:28:58,803 --> 00:29:02,407
I want to save her
no matter what she says.

450
00:29:07,645 --> 00:29:09,180
I won't just be there.

451
00:29:16,387 --> 00:29:18,389
I'll operate on her and cure her.

452
00:29:20,458 --> 00:29:21,326
Director...

453
00:29:22,727 --> 00:29:23,628
I'm begging you.

454
00:29:39,277 --> 00:29:40,111
Yes.

455
00:29:41,045 --> 00:29:42,013
I'm in.

456
00:29:42,247 --> 00:29:43,481
Thank you.

457
00:29:44,415 --> 00:29:45,383
Dr. Daimon.

458
00:29:46,684 --> 00:29:47,519
Fine.

459
00:29:48,920 --> 00:29:49,788
Dr. Hara,

460
00:29:50,789 --> 00:29:54,392
I understand your thoughts very well.

461
00:29:56,594 --> 00:29:57,428
Director...

462
00:29:59,430 --> 00:30:02,700
Dr. Hara...

463
00:30:03,868 --> 00:30:08,473
you made Mrs. Uchikanda lose face

464
00:30:09,774 --> 00:30:14,179
and caused a lot of trouble
for this hospital.

465
00:30:15,613 --> 00:30:20,552
Yet with great compassion,
I let you take a leave of absence

466
00:30:21,386 --> 00:30:24,455
with the most favorable conditions.

467
00:30:26,624 --> 00:30:28,626
Dr. Hara, am I

468
00:30:29,527 --> 00:30:34,098
to understand that you're
disregarding my generosity?

469
00:30:36,334 --> 00:30:38,703
Operate if you want to.

470
00:30:39,437 --> 00:30:43,007
But when it's over

471
00:30:44,242 --> 00:30:48,546
leave Totei University Hospital.

472
00:30:50,048 --> 00:30:51,015
Okay?

473
00:30:52,150 --> 00:30:55,887
Over the names of patients
awaiting surgery...

474
00:30:58,590 --> 00:30:59,958
Something like this...

475
00:31:03,061 --> 00:31:05,129
How dare you slam it down.

476
00:31:09,067 --> 00:31:11,569
But Director Hiruma,
I'm sure he was...

477
00:31:11,636 --> 00:31:13,805
What is it, Dr. Torii?

478
00:31:14,806 --> 00:31:15,740
Nothing, sir.

479
00:31:18,910 --> 00:31:21,412
Ah yes…Dr. Michiko Daimon.

480
00:31:22,313 --> 00:31:27,185
If you're going to be there for
Dr. Hara during the operation

481
00:31:27,785 --> 00:31:31,923
I'll immediately terminate
your contract with us.

482
00:31:32,123 --> 00:31:33,558
Keep that in mind.

483
00:31:36,628 --> 00:31:37,462
Dismissed.

484
00:31:47,805 --> 00:31:49,440
Nobody's moving?

485
00:32:12,597 --> 00:32:13,498
What are you doing?

486
00:32:13,765 --> 00:32:15,967
- We'll assist you.
- What?

487
00:32:16,134 --> 00:32:18,770
I want to watch
Dr. Daimon operate.

488
00:32:19,003 --> 00:32:20,571
Drs. Morimoto and Nishiyama...

489
00:32:21,506 --> 00:32:22,573
You could get fired.

490
00:32:22,740 --> 00:32:25,376
Then I'll be Dr. Daimon's
exclusive assistant.

491
00:32:25,944 --> 00:32:27,111
I decline.

492
00:32:31,783 --> 00:32:32,917
Wait for me.

493
00:32:44,195 --> 00:32:45,863
You're here?

494
00:32:46,698 --> 00:32:51,069
It's their last operation.
I wanted to watch how it ends.

495
00:32:52,971 --> 00:32:54,439
And you, Dr. Torii?

496
00:32:55,440 --> 00:32:56,374
No special reason.

497
00:32:56,841 --> 00:32:59,544
I doubt I'll be punished
for just watching.

498
00:33:17,028 --> 00:33:19,897
We're now starting
an awake craniotomy.

499
00:33:20,131 --> 00:33:21,332
Awake?

500
00:33:22,500 --> 00:33:23,735
Why?

501
00:33:23,801 --> 00:33:26,838
Wouldn't keeping her awake
increase the risks?

502
00:33:27,038 --> 00:33:30,675
A regular removal won't
guarantee her life as a surgeon.

503
00:33:31,075 --> 00:33:34,012
I'll make sure her hand
doesn't get paralyzed.

504
00:33:34,078 --> 00:33:35,113
Scalpel.

505
00:33:46,024 --> 00:33:47,291
Scalp clip.

506
00:33:47,492 --> 00:33:50,728
The tumor is pressing against
and invading the motor cortex.

507
00:33:51,929 --> 00:33:52,864
Can she handle this?

508
00:33:54,599 --> 00:33:55,600
Dr. Inomata.

509
00:33:56,334 --> 00:33:58,770
It sounds like you want her to succeed.

510
00:33:59,837 --> 00:34:03,708
Whether she succeeds or not,
it has nothing to do with me.

511
00:34:15,920 --> 00:34:18,089
SURGERY TIME

512
00:34:25,496 --> 00:34:26,931
They're waking her up.

513
00:34:43,247 --> 00:34:44,215
She's awake.

514
00:34:46,184 --> 00:34:47,452
Can you say your name?

515
00:34:48,486 --> 00:34:49,921
Nanasha Najinsky.

516
00:34:51,756 --> 00:34:53,091
There's no pain.

517
00:34:53,858 --> 00:34:55,860
Are my vitals normal?

518
00:34:56,427 --> 00:34:57,762
Yes, they are.

519
00:34:58,896 --> 00:35:01,265
You're so calm.

520
00:35:02,133 --> 00:35:03,134
Let's begin.

521
00:35:07,004 --> 00:35:12,376
I'm starting the stimulations so
open and close your right hand.

522
00:35:22,053 --> 00:35:22,954
No abnormalities.

523
00:35:24,055 --> 00:35:25,623
Setting resection line.

524
00:35:26,791 --> 00:35:28,025
- Here.
- Okay.

525
00:35:33,931 --> 00:35:35,266
This is the hard part.

526
00:35:35,500 --> 00:35:38,269
Removing the tumor without
affecting motor skills.

527
00:35:41,906 --> 00:35:42,740
Kin...

528
00:35:43,007 --> 00:35:44,175
give the tool to Nanasha.

529
00:35:44,375 --> 00:35:45,243
Okay.

530
00:35:45,309 --> 00:35:46,777
Get the sheet.

531
00:35:47,111 --> 00:35:47,945
Nana...

532
00:35:50,848 --> 00:35:52,950
Trace over the lines.

533
00:35:59,724 --> 00:36:00,858
Kin, how is she?

534
00:36:00,925 --> 00:36:03,094
Nana, how's your hand?

535
00:36:03,394 --> 00:36:04,595
Fine.

536
00:36:04,996 --> 00:36:05,863
It looks good.

537
00:36:06,430 --> 00:36:07,431
Right here.

538
00:36:17,642 --> 00:36:19,777
Contractions on the right side.

539
00:36:20,444 --> 00:36:21,879
Frequent brain wave spikes.

540
00:36:22,013 --> 00:36:23,481
Cool the surface. Hurry.

541
00:36:23,614 --> 00:36:25,016
Pulse 140.

542
00:36:25,216 --> 00:36:27,285
Administer 10 mg of diazepam.

543
00:36:27,351 --> 00:36:29,353
- Saline.
- One more.

544
00:36:35,026 --> 00:36:36,227
Mamo...

545
00:36:41,132 --> 00:36:42,066
Mamo...

546
00:36:44,135 --> 00:36:45,770
We didn't make it to Kanazawa.

547
00:36:46,070 --> 00:36:47,538
Don't talk.

548
00:36:50,274 --> 00:36:54,679
Thanks for bringing me
back to the hospital.

549
00:36:58,482 --> 00:37:00,551
I wish I could live.

550
00:37:09,794 --> 00:37:10,861
Mamo...

551
00:37:18,803 --> 00:37:19,670
Nana...

552
00:37:30,548 --> 00:37:32,016
Pulse down to 100.

553
00:37:34,018 --> 00:37:35,553
We'll continue
when she's awake.

554
00:37:37,855 --> 00:37:39,323
Let's stop the operation.

555
00:37:44,028 --> 00:37:44,962
Her life...

556
00:37:46,831 --> 00:37:48,332
Let's save her life first.

557
00:37:49,900 --> 00:37:50,968
Daimon!

558
00:37:51,369 --> 00:37:52,603
Don't push your luck.

559
00:37:53,504 --> 00:37:56,340
She'll be lucky if she stays alive.

560
00:37:57,308 --> 00:37:58,709
Continuing awake craniotomy.

561
00:37:58,843 --> 00:38:00,111
Dr. Daimon!

562
00:38:00,177 --> 00:38:02,813
I'll keep her alive as a surgeon too.

563
00:38:02,880 --> 00:38:03,814
But...

564
00:38:03,914 --> 00:38:06,317
I never fail.

565
00:38:09,487 --> 00:38:10,721
Wrap up in five minutes.

566
00:38:11,822 --> 00:38:13,691
Kin, stimulate the surface.

567
00:38:13,958 --> 00:38:15,826
What? Me?

568
00:38:17,328 --> 00:38:18,796
You're going to cure her, right?

569
00:38:30,574 --> 00:38:31,409
Yes.

570
00:38:32,977 --> 00:38:33,844
Dr. Daimon...

571
00:38:34,945 --> 00:38:37,381
My name is Mamoru Hara.

572
00:38:38,883 --> 00:38:39,817
Here.

573
00:38:42,787 --> 00:38:45,056
Nanasha, trace the lines again.

574
00:38:45,623 --> 00:38:46,457
Okay.

575
00:38:56,167 --> 00:38:57,435
She's doing it well.

576
00:38:57,601 --> 00:38:58,703
Now this one.

577
00:38:58,936 --> 00:39:00,771
Looking good.

578
00:39:07,611 --> 00:39:10,614
SURGERY TIME

579
00:39:23,928 --> 00:39:25,363
Tumor removed.

580
00:39:37,508 --> 00:39:38,342
All clear.

581
00:39:38,976 --> 00:39:39,810
Yes!

582
00:39:42,380 --> 00:39:45,549
She needs follow-up but
she can hold a scalpel again.

583
00:39:46,384 --> 00:39:47,218
Great.

584
00:39:50,988 --> 00:39:53,524
Welcome back, Dr. Najinsky.

585
00:40:00,264 --> 00:40:01,365
A brilliant operation.

586
00:40:03,734 --> 00:40:06,303
Brilliant or not, they're fired.

587
00:40:07,438 --> 00:40:10,541
So I'll say I'm glad it was successful.

588
00:40:19,817 --> 00:40:21,786
Finished. Blood loss?

589
00:40:21,886 --> 00:40:22,953
80 cc.

590
00:40:30,461 --> 00:40:31,295
Dr. Daimon...

591
00:40:32,997 --> 00:40:33,931
Thank you.

592
00:40:37,034 --> 00:40:38,002
Good job...

593
00:40:38,803 --> 00:40:39,637
Good job.

594
00:40:51,916 --> 00:40:54,618
Dr. Hara turned down
the arranged marriage?

595
00:40:55,519 --> 00:40:58,722
Just imagine what
Mrs. Uchikanda will say.

596
00:41:00,024 --> 00:41:01,425
Hello.

597
00:41:01,859 --> 00:41:02,827
Director Hiruma.

598
00:41:03,327 --> 00:41:07,465
Thank you for employing
Daimon from our agency.

599
00:41:07,731 --> 00:41:09,233
Melon.

600
00:41:10,301 --> 00:41:11,769
The bill.

601
00:41:12,369 --> 00:41:13,270
This time for sure

602
00:41:13,938 --> 00:41:18,542
I will not pay you a single penny.

603
00:41:18,742 --> 00:41:20,444
Why do you say that?

604
00:41:20,811 --> 00:41:24,114
The four surgeons
including Dr. Michiko Daimon

605
00:41:24,648 --> 00:41:28,252
who participated in that operation

606
00:41:29,053 --> 00:41:30,654
will be fired.

607
00:41:31,288 --> 00:41:33,924
Oh…Is that right?

608
00:41:34,825 --> 00:41:39,063
Then what should I do with this?

609
00:41:39,497 --> 00:41:41,131
WITH APPRECIATION

610
00:41:41,398 --> 00:41:43,067
From Chairman Uchikanda?

611
00:41:43,567 --> 00:41:47,404
I just met with Chairman Uchikanda.

612
00:41:47,905 --> 00:41:52,243
He wants you to have this
as a token of his appreciation.

613
00:41:53,110 --> 00:41:55,112
Hennessy?
From the chairman?

614
00:41:55,179 --> 00:41:56,013
Yes.

615
00:41:56,247 --> 00:41:57,214
Why?

616
00:41:57,982 --> 00:42:00,317
For some time now

617
00:42:00,451 --> 00:42:03,854
Chairman Uchikanda had
been looking for a way to

618
00:42:04,188 --> 00:42:06,891
make connections with
the American Medical Club.

619
00:42:07,291 --> 00:42:12,630
Now he can do so after
Totei saved the life of

620
00:42:12,863 --> 00:42:18,135
Nanasha Najinsky, the daughter
of their vice chairman.

621
00:42:18,335 --> 00:42:19,937
He's ecstatic.

622
00:42:21,572 --> 00:42:26,644
So now he owes us a big favor
in return for this operation?

623
00:42:26,911 --> 00:42:28,145
That's right.

624
00:42:28,579 --> 00:42:32,016
Well, this is a surprising
turn of events.

625
00:42:32,650 --> 00:42:35,185
You have a call from
Chairman Uchikanda.

626
00:42:35,819 --> 00:42:37,187
From the chairman?

627
00:42:38,188 --> 00:42:39,757
This is Hiruma.

628
00:42:41,025 --> 00:42:43,427
Is that so? I see.

629
00:42:43,561 --> 00:42:47,898
Thank you very much.
I appreciate your call.

630
00:42:50,401 --> 00:42:52,836
A thank-you call from
Chairman Uchikanda?

631
00:42:52,970 --> 00:42:53,804
Yes.

632
00:42:55,239 --> 00:42:57,675
How about showing your appreciation

633
00:42:59,343 --> 00:43:01,512
to Daimon and me?

634
00:43:02,846 --> 00:43:03,747
$100,000?

635
00:43:04,448 --> 00:43:05,282
With pleasure.

636
00:43:06,250 --> 00:43:07,818
Thank you.

637
00:43:08,285 --> 00:43:12,790
Dr. Hara is turning down
his marriage with Momoka.

638
00:43:13,757 --> 00:43:18,395
Make sure he gets what he deserves
for humiliating me.

639
00:43:19,563 --> 00:43:20,798
I decline.

640
00:43:21,832 --> 00:43:22,866
Excuse me?

641
00:43:23,133 --> 00:43:26,604
It was decided by Totei
under my husband's leadership.

642
00:43:27,571 --> 00:43:30,507
You're an outsider after all.

643
00:43:31,475 --> 00:43:33,143
Good day.

644
00:43:34,044 --> 00:43:34,878
Hey.

645
00:43:35,813 --> 00:43:36,680
Stop!

646
00:43:38,782 --> 00:43:41,952
The best moment in my life.

647
00:43:50,060 --> 00:43:53,631
I'm glad you're doing
so well post-op.

648
00:43:55,532 --> 00:43:58,369
I owe it to everybody
who operated on me.

649
00:44:01,538 --> 00:44:02,406
Nana...

650
00:44:04,441 --> 00:44:06,443
Do you want me to go with you?

651
00:44:08,846 --> 00:44:11,382
I'm not getting fired from Totei.

652
00:44:11,782 --> 00:44:16,720
But I can also become freelance
and go to the States with you.

653
00:44:17,888 --> 00:44:20,924
It's a big decision for me.

654
00:44:21,759 --> 00:44:25,963
But if you want me
to be there for you...

655
00:44:26,030 --> 00:44:28,232
Stop it.

656
00:44:29,900 --> 00:44:30,834
What?

657
00:44:30,901 --> 00:44:34,672
A real doctor is one that
never fails an operation.

658
00:44:35,105 --> 00:44:36,340
Being there doesn't count.

659
00:44:37,307 --> 00:44:38,342
Doesn't count?

660
00:44:38,609 --> 00:44:40,444
But you said you loved me.

661
00:44:41,278 --> 00:44:43,814
Bye-bye, Kin.

662
00:44:45,816 --> 00:44:46,884
But you said...

663
00:44:47,651 --> 00:44:48,485
Hey!

664
00:44:49,853 --> 00:44:51,188
My name's not Kin!

665
00:44:51,889 --> 00:44:55,225
Nana! Be there for me!

666
00:44:56,794 --> 00:45:00,831
Come back!!!

667
00:45:02,466 --> 00:45:04,802
Thank you, Mamo.

668
00:45:09,406 --> 00:45:13,477
<i>Despising the herd mentality, authority</i>
<i>and institutional restraints...</i>

669
00:45:13,977 --> 00:45:19,183
<i>Her solo weapons are her license</i>
<i>and the skills she has acquired.</i>

670
00:45:21,018 --> 00:45:23,253
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon.</i>

671
00:45:23,787 --> 00:45:25,055
<i>Also known as...</i>

672
00:45:25,355 --> 00:45:26,990
<i>Doctor-X.</i>

673
00:45:27,057 --> 00:45:28,992
THIS DRAMA IS FICTION

674
00:45:29,426 --> 00:45:30,461
Who are you?

675
00:45:30,527 --> 00:45:31,595
Don't be rude.

676
00:45:31,729 --> 00:45:33,163
Hiruma!

677
00:45:33,230 --> 00:45:34,331
An unwavering resolve.

678
00:45:34,398 --> 00:45:36,433
If I don't perform your operation,
you will die.

679
00:45:36,500 --> 00:45:38,435
- Don't let her perform the operation.
- Yes sir.

680
00:45:38,502 --> 00:45:40,170
I want to save patients' lives, too.

681
00:45:40,237 --> 00:45:41,071
The patient is going to die.

682
00:45:41,138 --> 00:45:43,841
A doctor should never fail.
